---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { translations } from '../i18n/translations';

const t = translations.en;
const githubUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GITHUB_URL;
const homeUrl = 'https://fntx.modone.me/';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  currentPath="privacy"
  title={t.seo.privacy.title}
  description={t.seo.privacy.description}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 px-4 py-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 sm:px-6 dark:text-slate-400">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: t.breadcrumb.home, href: homeUrl }, { label: t.footer.links.privacy }]} />

    <header class="space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">
        Privacy Policy: Your Fonts Stay on Your Computer
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Last updated: November 26, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Your font files are never uploaded. They are opened and processed inside your own browser.
        We only remember your theme and language choice on your device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Your font files</h2>
      <p>
        When you drop a font into the workbench, it is read into your browser’s memory and handled
        there. Generated files are created on your device too. Closing or refreshing the page clears
        this data. We do not receive, store, or inspect your fonts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Settings saved on your device
      </h2>
      <p>
        We use browser <code>localStorage</code> for two preferences: light/dark theme and interface
        language. These values stay on your device and contain no personal identity information. You
        can clear them at any time in your browser settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Hosting logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider may keep standard access logs such as IP address,
        time, and page requested for security and reliability. These logs do not contain your font
        files.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Ads and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The site does not currently use advertising or analytics cookies. If advertising (for
        example Google AdSense) is enabled in the future, we will ask for consent first, and those
        providers may use cookies under their own policies. This page will be updated before that
        happens.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What we do not do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not require an account, do not sell personal data, and do not use your fonts to train
        anything.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy?
        {githubUrl ? (
          <a href={githubUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-slate-100">
            Open an issue on GitHub
          </a>
        ) : (
          <span>Use the contact link in the site footer when available.</span>
        )}
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>